Human AML	 	Various genetic aberrations, including t(8;21), inv(16), t(15;17), t(11q23), complex karyotype, whole bone marrow cells are from <a href="https://tcga-data.nci.nih.gov/tcga/tcgaHome2.jsp" target="_blank">The Cancer Genome Atlas (TCGA)</a><br>
AML cells are compared to their nearest normal counterpart, as described in <a href="http://www.bloodjournal.org/content/123/6/894.short?sso-checked=true" target="_blank">Rapin et al. <i>Blood</i>, 2014</a><br><br>
